cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Reproducing RetinexDual: an independent reproduction on UHD-LL"
message: >-
  If you refer to this reproduction, please cite it using the metadata below.
  If you are citing the model itself rather than this reproduction, cite the
  RetinexDual paper under references, not this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jack
    family-names: Wu
    alias: lemoon01110
repository-code: "https://github.com/lemoon01110/Reproducing-RetinexDual"
abstract: >-
  An independent reproduction of RetinexDual (Kishawy, Hussein and Chen, ICPR
  2026) on the UHD-LL low-light benchmark. The published PSNR reproduces at
  28.8199 +/- 0.0027 dB over five seeds and 150 images, against 28.79 reported.
  The published SSIM does not reproduce, coming out 0.0118 low, and testing six
  SSIM conventions did not account for the gap. The report also documents three
  undocumented defects that prevent a clean checkout of the released code from
  running, two further traps that run to completion while returning a wrong
  number, a revision mismatch between the released checkpoint and the released
  code, and the unguarded Gumbel sampling that makes default inference
  nondeterministic.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - reproduction study
  - low-light image enhancement
  - image restoration
  - state space models
  - pytorch
license: MIT
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      RetinexDual: Retinex-based Dual Nature Approach for Generalized
      Ultra-High-Definition Image Restoration
    authors:
